          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Q.3. Are there other ways to arrange the data?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.104,
            0.591,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": "Ans. Yes, the data can be arranged in a frequency table."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.153,
            0.218,
            0.17
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Section 4.2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.185,
            0.227,
            0.203
          ],
          "content": "**Page No. 83**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.216,
            0.881,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": "**Q. What could be the problems faced in preparing such a pictograph, if the total number of students present in a class is 33 or 27?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.267,
            0.881,
            0.306
          ],
          "content": "Ans. represents 10 students and represent 5 students. But to represent 3 or 7 students accurately by dividing these symbols is not possible."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.351,
            0.238,
            0.369
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.378,
            0.882,
            0.413
          ],
          "content": "**Q.1. The following pictograph shows the number of books borrowed by students, in a week, from the library of Middle School, Ginnori —**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.423,
            0.73,
            0.441
          ],
          "content": "**a. On which day were the minimum number of books borrowed?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.45,
            0.748,
            0.468
          ],
          "content": "**b. What was the total number of books borrowed during the week?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.477,
            0.881,
            0.513
          ],
          "content": "**c. On which day were the maximum number of books borrowed? What may be the possible reason?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.523,
            0.28,
            0.539
          ],
          "content": "Ans. a. Thursday"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.54,
            0.226,
            0.556
          ],
          "content": "b. 24"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.558,
            0.881,
            0.593
          ],
          "content": "c. Saturday. One of the reasons could be that Sunday being a holiday students can read the borrowed books on Sunday."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.607,
            0.883,
            0.661
          ],
          "content": "**Q.2. Magan Bhai sells kites at Jamnagar. Six shopkeepers from nearby villages come to purchase kites from him. The number of kites he sold to these six shopkeepers are given below —**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.673,
            0.712,
            0.693
          ],
          "content": "**Prepare a pictograph using the symbol** T **to represent 100 kites.**"
        },
